WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.990
In Mark, Jesus sends out his twelve disciples
with authority over unclean spirits.

2
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.350
They cast out many demons.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.830
Later, he comes down
a mountain with Peter,

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.500
James and John.

5
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.910
Below, a crowd is arguing.

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.040
A father has brought his son.

7
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.530
Since childhood, a spirit has
thrown the boy into fire and water.

8
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.830
And the disciples have tried to free him.

9
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.310
They were not able.

10
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.860
So what went wrong for
Jesus' own disciples?

11
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.950
In this mission, you'll see why Mark
presents Jesus' exorcisms as a battle against

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.890
evil.

13
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.050
Then you'll compare how Christians and
Humanists understand exorcism today.

14
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.070
Your mission: find out what went wrong
when Jesus' disciples failed to free the

15
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.210
suffering boy.
